      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-297563",
      ":question/problem": "A survey was conducted among $160$ employees at a manufacturing plant. The table below shows the number of employees who work either the day shift or the night shift, grouped by whether they are salaried or hourly workers.\n\n| Employment Type | Day Shift | Night Shift | Total |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Salaried | $32$ | $8$ | $40$ |\n| Hourly | $58$ | $62$ | $120$ |\n| **Total** | **$90$** | **$70$** | **$160$** |\n\nIf one employee is selected at random, what is the probability that the selected employee is an hourly worker?"
